/**
 * LOGIC RATIONALE:
 *   Extractiveness is high (0.82) and rises monotonically from 0.58 across the interval because the constraint transfers interpretive authority from local practitioners to Buddhist institutional hierarchy without equivalent return in institutional autonomy. Early adoption by elite Tendai/Shingon circles generated lower extractiveness (0.58 — more voluntary, less enforced); systematization and state reinforcement raised extractiveness as the doctrine became Buddhist orthodoxy (final value 0.82). Suppression is substantial (0.71) because persistence depends on actively excluding alternative readings from institutional authority (what would domain-partition advocates propose? what would pragmatic-incoherence advocates claim?) and reinterpreting indigenous narratives as misunderstandings rather than legitimate alternatives. Theater ratio rises monotonically to 0.58 and plateaus because as the doctrine matured, growing share of enforcement activity is textual commentary and scholastic argument (performative maintenance of metaphysical truth) rather than functional coordination. Accessibility collapse is moderate (0.73) because practitioners could in principle adopt alternatives, but institutional barriers (control of temples, education, prestige positions) make alternatives costly; local folk communities sometimes sustained kami-autonomy framings despite institutional suppression. Resistance is substantial (0.68) because indigenous practitioners and alternative-reading advocates continuously object to the monopoly, though suppressed rather than militarily crushed. The measurement series all share the single time grid (t=0 to t=40) so temporal analysis has coherent data; no metric is authored at different endpoints.
 *
 * PERSPECTIVAL GAP:
 *   Buddhist institutional seat and indigenous kami practitioner seat should compute radically different types from the engine. From institutional Buddhist seat: this is genuine coordination. Honji-suijaku solves the logical coherence problem and provides an elegant metaphysical framework practitioners appreciate (they experience the constraint as intellectual unification). The constraint's work is real — it enables simultaneous practice without contradiction. From indigenous seat: the same structure operates as enforced interpretive subordination. Kami autonomy is overridden, shrine authority is absorbed, and practitioners are told their own understanding is metaphysically mistaken. The constraint's work is authority extraction disguised as truth discovery. The engine computes this divergence from structural data: institutional seat is (institutional power + arbitrage exit + agenda-setter role) → lower directionality (beneficiary range); indigenous seat is (moderate power + identity-locked exit + victim role) → higher directionality (target range). The structural asymmetry is authored explicitly; the engine computes per-seat types from it. The claim/metric independence rule is key here: honji-suijaku is CLAIMED as tangled_rope (has coordination + asymmetric extraction). The metrics describe high extractiveness and suppression. If the engine computed this as snare or rope, that divergence is the measurement the corpus exists to take.
 *
 * DIRECTIONALITY LOGIC:
 *   Buddhist institutional hierarchy: Beneficiary seat. Power is institutional (control temple networks, textual transmission, ordination authority), exit is arbitrage (could adopt alternatives but at career cost), role is agenda-setter (sets the doctrine, enforces through institutional authority). Directionality d near 0.10 (full beneficiary leaning) — they collect interpretive authority and institutional prestige; the constraint's benefits accrue to them. The beneficiary declaration captures this structural position. Indigenous kami practitioners: Victim seat. Power is moderate (can mount community resistance but lack institutional platform), exit is identity-locked (cannot abandon kami veneration without losing self-concept and community), role is victim (bear the cost of interpretive subordination). Directionality d near 0.90 (near-full target) — they bear the extraction (loss of explanatory autonomy, reinterpretation of their practice); the constraint operates on them. The victim declaration captures this. Local shrine autonomy: Victim-adjacent seat. Power is moderate, exit is constrained (refusal means marginalization), role is payer (loses autonomous authority). Directionality d near 0.85-0.90. Buddhist scholars: Beneficiary seat with mobile exit. Power is institutional, exit is mobile (can leave by adopting alternatives), role is beneficiary (prestige/career advancement). Directionality d near 0.25-0.30 (beneficiary with visible exit) — override from structural derivation (~0.18) to 0.12 to reflect that while they profit from the framework, exit is more available than pure beneficiary would suggest; their d reflects that. Lay practitioners: Hybrid seat near symmetric. Power is powerless, exit is constrained, role is beneficiary + payer (both gain coordination value and lose interpretive authority). Directionality d near 0.45-0.55 (symmetric with asymmetric components) — they benefit and pay roughly equally, but the asymmetry is that the benefit is automatic while the payment is enforced.
 *
 * MANDATROPHY ANALYSIS:
 *   The tangled_rope classification prevents false natural-law misreading and false pure-extraction misreading. If this were labeled mountain: the framework would claim honji-suijaku is unchangeable natural law, that simultaneous veneration necessarily requires this doctrine, that the constraint would persist regardless of institutional enforcement. False natural-law reading. The extracted ε (0.82) and suppression (0.71) make this implausible; the Meiji refutation (constraint collapsed when institutional enforcement shifted) proves it is not natural law. If this were labeled snare: the classification would claim no genuine coordination function, that the entire arrangement is extraction justified by false universality claim. But practitioners genuinely experience intellectual coherence and logical unification from honji-suijaku — this is not all cover story. The coordination is real even though it is asymmetric. Tangled_rope correctly names both: the constraint solves a genuine logical problem (coordination function is real) AND it asymmetrically transfers authority from indigenous to institutional Buddhist seats (extraction is real). The measurement series reinforces this: early high coordination value (extractiveness rising from 0.58 suggests accumulating extraction overlaid on coordination foundation), theater ratio plateauing at 0.58 (doctrinal elaboration is performative maintenance, not functional adaptation), suppression remaining high (enforcement required to exclude alternatives indicates coordination is enforced, not voluntary). A piton reading would claim the function has atrophied and only performance remains — but the coordination (resolution of logical incoherence problem) remains functionally vital, so piton does not fit.
 */

